  "explain_en": "In a construction environment, experienced workers (veterans) always give top priority to maintaining construction quality and ensuring safety for themselves and their colleagues. Always being conscious of safety rules and technical standards helps prevent work accidents and ensures the final product achieves the highest quality required by the project.\n\nVocabulary:\n建設現場(けんせつげんば) (Construction site): The place where construction activities take place.\n技能者(ぎのうしゃ) (Skilled worker/Craftsperson): A person who does specialized work.\n常に(つねに) (Always): A state maintained continuously.\n意識(いしき) (Awareness/Attention): Recognizing and paying attention.\n事項(じこう) (Item/Matter): Work items.\n新しい(あたらしい) (New): Something that has just appeared.\n技術(ぎじゅつ) (Technique/Technology): A specialized method.\n学ぶ(まなぶ) (To learn): To acquire knowledge.\n高い(たかい) (High): A large degree.\n品質(ひんしつ) (Quality): The value of a product.\n安全(あんぜん) (Safety): A state with no danger.\n確保(かくほ) (To secure/ensure): To keep something certain.\n強化(きょうか) (Strengthening): Making something stronger.\n効率的(こうりつてき) (Efficient): Completing work with little waste.\n作業(さぎょう) (Work): Construction operations.\n行う(おこなう) (To carry out): To perform an action.",
